# Rule: git and pull requests

- Follow the repository's existing conventions: look at `git log` and open pull requests for branch names and commit message style, and copy them.
- Agents never commit, push, reset, stash or change git configuration. A human reviews `git diff` and commits.
- One feature per branch and pull request; reference the feature id (`FEAT-xxx`).
- A pull request says what changed and why, and pastes the summary of `.ai/evidence/latest/report.md`.
- Never force-push a shared branch. Never commit `.env`, keys or build output.
